The current Authorised Persons list is displayed on the noticeboard in the workshop and is available electronically on the shared drive (path: TWA/Operations/Maintenance/Authorised Persons).

1.4.4 Refresher Training

Refresher training shall be undertaken as follows:

| Training | Frequency | Delivered By |
|----------|-----------|--------------|
| First Aid at Work | Every 3 years | External provider |
| Manual Handling | Every 2 years | In-house |
| Working at Height | Every 2 years | In-house |
| Confined Space Entry | Annually | External provider |
| Lockout/Tagout | Annually | In-house |
| Safe Use of Chemicals | Annually | In-house |

Refresher training shall be completed during working hours. Time spent on refresher training shall be recorded on the individual’s timesheet using the code TRN.

1.4.5 New Starters and Returners

New starters shall complete a structured induction programme before carrying out any maintenance work. The induction programme covers:

- Site safety rules and emergency procedures;
- Location of first aid equipment and fire extinguishers;
- Introduction to the key plant areas;
- Use of the permit-to-work system;
- Introduction to this manual and how to use it.

The induction programme shall be completed within the first two weeks of employment. A record of completion shall be signed by both the new starter and the Maintenance Supervisor.

Individuals returning from a period of absence of more than six months (including maternity leave, paternity leave, or long-term sickness) shall complete a return-to-work assessment. The return-to-work assessment shall include a review of any changes to procedures or plant that have taken place during the absence, and a practical assessment of the individual’s competence in their core tasks.

1.4.6 Dennis Okafor – Certification Record

Dennis Okafor's certification is NVQ Level 3 in Maintenance Operations. Record status: current. This certification is current and is held on file in the Administrative Support office. Dennis also holds a current IOSH Managing Safely certificate and has completed the in-house planning and scheduling course.

Dennis’s competency assessments are up to date for the following tasks:

- Planned maintenance of centrifugal pumps;
- Planned maintenance of air compressors;
- Fault diagnosis on MCC panels;
- Permit-to-work authorisation (as issuer);
- Lockout/tagout (as senior authorised person).

Any changes to Dennis’s certification status shall be reported to the Operations Manager in writing.

1.4.7 Training Records

Training records shall be maintained for each individual and shall include:

- Copies of all certificates;
- Records of competency assessments;
- Records of refresher training;
- Records of any training needs identified during performance reviews.

Training records are confidential and shall be stored in a locked cabinet in the Administrative Support office. Electronic copies shall be stored on the shared drive in a restricted folder (path: TWA/HR/Training Records). Access to the electronic copies shall be restricted to the Administrative Support team, the Operations Manager, and the individual concerned.

1.4.8 Training Needs Identification

Training needs shall be identified through:

- Annual performance reviews;
- Changes to plant or equipment;
- Changes to legislation or industry guidance;
- Incident investigations;
- Observations of poor practice.

Training needs shall be recorded on Form TW/TNI/01 and submitted to the Works Maintenance Planner. The Works Maintenance Planner shall prioritise training needs based on risk and shall include them in the annual training plan.
